Here, if one more count is added, because

271
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:23,120
when it turns on, it is counted on the rising edge.

272
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:27,519
If it turns on here, bring another count

273
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:31,959
into the counter, and one count is added.

274
00:14:27,519 --> 00:14:34,440
This continues. Until when?

275
00:14:31,959 --> 00:14:37,440
Until Timer 2 reaches the counter period

276
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:39,360
or the overflow value.

277
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:42,880
Okay, now

278
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:45,839
therefore, this is repeated

279
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:49,160
so that one, two, three, and so on

280
00:14:45,839 --> 00:14:52,120
keep increasing until it reaches the value

281
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:54,880
of its own overflow

282
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:56,839
or its maximum value.

283
00:14:54,880 --> 00:15:03,000
Now I will build the program

284
00:14:56,839 --> 00:15:03,000
so it can run, and for the first

285
00:15:03,079 --> 00:15:10,160
time this value

286
00:15:05,959 --> 00:15:15,120
will take a little time. Now we load

287
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:19,079
our program.

288
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:21,360
In this section we also press Load so that the program

289
00:15:19,079 --> 00:15:26,600
is loaded onto the microcontroller. Then we

290
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:30,920
open the STM Studio program

291
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:32,519
like this.

292
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:35,440
In the File section we select Import Variable.

293
00:15:32,519 --> 00:15:40,199
We select Import Variable, and in the

294
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:40,199
Desktop section

295
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:48,399
we see the project we created, the Counter project,

296
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:50,240
in the STM32 folder.

297
00:15:48,399 --> 00:15:52,319
Counter Utility, and we select the file

298
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:55,480
with the .axf extension.

299
00:15:52,319 --> 00:15:58,120
Then we can select all these parameters.

300
00:15:55,480 --> 00:16:00,600
We select the parameter named counter

301
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:04,600
so that the counter output

302
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:04,600
is placed into it, and we import it.

303
00:16:04,759 --> 00:16:11,160
And in this section

304
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:13,160
we right-click, select Scope, and here

305
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:18,240
we can display it as a bar graph or

306
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:20,360
as a table. I will display it as a table.

307
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:23,040
Now I press the microcontroller Reset button

308
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:26,360
to run the program, and

309
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:30,120
here I press Run. As you can see,

310
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:33,519
every 100 milliseconds

311
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:37,560
one is being added to it. You can see

312
00:16:33,519 --> 00:16:40,639
until it reaches a value of 100.

313
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:45,120
So the project works like this: every 100 milliseconds

314
00:16:40,639 --> 00:16:47,079
for which we configured the timer, PC13

315
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:50,519
turns off and on, and with this switching

316
00:16:47,079 --> 00:16:52,680
the counter value, the value entering

317
00:16:50,519 --> 00:16:56,880
the counter input

318
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:59,920
at PA0 is counted, and the counter

319
00:16:56,880 --> 00:17:03,120
keeps counting and increasing, and this value

320
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:06,919
is placed into this counter.

321
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:09,480
To display it, as it increases and is counted

322
00:17:06,919 --> 00:17:11,799
one by one, every 100 milliseconds you can see here

323
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:15,679
that the counter increases its value by one

324
00:17:11,799 --> 00:17:18,079
every 100 milliseconds, and this value continues

325
00:17:15,679 --> 00:17:21,199
to increase until our second timer

326
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:23,240
reaches its overflow value, which is 100, and then

327
00:17:21,199 --> 00:17:25,640
returns to zero.

328
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:25,640
Goodbye.
